# LinkedIn graphics (Mike + Doc)

Keep **Mike, Doc, and the illustration style**. Change **composition and scenery** to fit the post. Do not clone the last graphic or always use the same London consult room.

## House style (constant)

- Square 1:1 (~1080x1080). Forest-green + cream. Flat cartoon line-art.
- Characters from `services/ai-studio/input/mike-and-doc.png`.
- Perfect spelling. No hashtags, URLs, logos, or prompt labels (`Eyebrow:`, `Title:`).
- Generate with Gemini via `services/ai-studio`.

## Scenery (must vary)

Match the **place** to the post. Do not default to Big Ben windows every time.

- Treatment decision / evidence talk → clinic consult room
- Early mobilisation / loading → physio gym, corridor, or walking practice
- First weeks / protect the repair → hospital ward or first walk with crutches
- Boot coming off / gait → marked walkway or gait lab, unused boot on the side
- After independent walking → outdoor path past a walking milestone, more road ahead
- Return to sport → gym, track, or outdoor path
- Sleep / night splint → bedroom
- Exam / special test → treatment plinth, close-up
- Imaging / tendon monitoring → ultrasound room (keep it cartoon, no fake scan numbers)

London details can appear sometimes, not always.

## Layout (must vary)

Pick a structure that matches **this post’s idea**, not a default template.

Examples:
- Trade-off / evidence → balance scale, two paths, or a large comparison board
- Process / rehab → timeline, steps on the floor, walking sequence
- Test / exam → close-up of the test, two poses side by side
- Myth vs evidence → split beat, not three identical footer cards
- Return to sport → action pose, checklist in Doc’s hands, not another consult chair

**Do not reuse** “Doc left + Mike on chair + whiteboard + three bottom cards + green pill” unless that is genuinely the best fit. The Achilles `*-v3.png` trio is one look, not the only look.

## Do not do this

- Canva split: boxed photo on the left, stacked white cards on the right
- Typographic SVG-only grids with no characters, unless the user asks for no characters
- Giant comedy props, mad-scientist Doc, or invented statistics

## Characters

- **Doc:** older, balding, white hair at sides, white beard, round glasses, Thetis-green scrubs, green crocs, yellow clipboard.
- **Mike:** 40s, slim, short brown hair, white t-shirt, blue jeans.
- **Achilles rupture:** ONE walking boot on the injured foot, white sneaker on the other.
- **Plantar fasciitis / heel pain:** no boot, no cast. White sneakers on both feet.
